## 4. Next Steps for Implementation

To operationalize this phase locally, the DevOps team must create the standard deployment manifest and the promotion script that bridges the gap between the DevOps pipeline and the Security team's proxy.

1. **Create the Manifest:** `DevOps/k8s/production-deployment.yaml`
   ```yaml
   apiVersion: v1
   kind: ServiceAccount
   metadata:
     name: secure-app-sa
     namespace: production-workloads
   automountServiceAccountToken: false # Strictly limits API access
   ---
   apiVersion: apps/v1
   kind: Deployment
   metadata:
     name: trusted-app-production
     namespace: production-workloads
   spec:
     replicas: 1
     selector:
       matchLabels:
         app: trusted-app
     template:
       metadata:
         labels:
           app: trusted-app
       spec:
         serviceAccountName: secure-app-sa
         # Notice: runtimeClassName is explicitly omitted here to use containerd
         containers:
         - name: app-container
           image: local-devops-build:latest
           ports:
           - containerPort: 8080
   ---
   apiVersion: v1
   kind: Service
   metadata:
     name: trusted-app-svc
     namespace: production-workloads
   spec:
     type: NodePort
     selector:
       app: trusted-app
     ports:
       - port: 8080
         targetPort: 8080
         nodePort: 30080


Create the Script: DevOps/scripts/04-production-promotion.sh

Bash
#!/bin/bash
echo "Starting Phase 4: Production Promotion & Proxy Handoff..."

echo "Creating production namespace and deploying trusted container..."
kubectl create namespace production-workloads
kubectl apply -f DevOps/k8s/production-deployment.yaml

echo "Forwarding traffic from Minikube to localhost:8080..."
# Run port-forwarding in the background
kubectl port-forward service/trusted-app-svc 8080:8080 -n production-workloads &

echo "Updating Security Proxy Configuration..."
# Assuming yq is installed to modify YAML locally
yq e '.listeners[0].backend_addr = "127.0.0.1:8080"' -i Security/proxy_config.yaml
yq e '.listeners[0].enabled = true' -i Security/proxy_config.yaml

echo "Restarting the Next-Gen IDS/IPS Go Agent..."
pkill -f "ngfw-monitor" || true
cd Security && go run main.go &

echo "Phase 4 Complete! Application is now live and protected by the eBPF/L7 Proxy."
echo "Users can now securely access the app at http://localhost         